But looking at `QBuffer::readData`:
```cpp
qint64 QBuffer::readData(char *data, qint64 len)
{
    Q_D(QBuffer);
    if ((len = qMin(len, qint64(d->buf->size()) - pos())) <= 0)
        return qint64(0);
    memcpy(data, d->buf->constData() + pos(), len);
    return len;
}
```

It returns the number of bytes read, which could be a partial count. So `readRawData` returns the partial count.

